data: {"id":"gen-1785177601-Q9kE2qjAwTQxa2yYaLnv","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1785177601,"model":"openai/gpt-5.6-terra","provider":"OpenAI","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"","role":"assistant","annotations":[{"type":"url_citation","url_citation":{"url":"https://github.com/traefik/traefik/pull/12167","title":"Add least time load balancing strategy","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"# Add least time load balancing strategy\n\n- State: merged\n- Author: sdelicata\n- Created: 2025-10-17T13:40:23Z\n- Updated: 2025-10-23T14:16:07Z\n- Repository: traefik/traefik\n- Number: #12167\n- +1830 -134 in 25 files\n- Merged: 2025-10-23T14:16:05Z\n- Merge commit: a754236ce501b63560cf241830bbe22cd1695f0e\n\n[...]\n\n> :no_entry_sign: checks status: PR status: cancelled\n\n- traefiker added label \"bot/need-human-merge\"\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- someone committed\n\n- rtribotte head_ref_force_pushed\n\n- rtribotte removed label \"bot/need-human-merge\"\n\n- traefiker merged\n\n- traefiker closed\n\n- traefiker removed label \"status/3-needs-merge\"\n\n- Referenced by issue #1550: Initial support for Traefik Proxy v3.6.0\n\n[...]\n\n**traefiker** commented on 2025-10-23T09:58:04Z:\n\n[...]\n\n- area/provider/\n\n[...]\n\n### What does this PR do? \n \nAdds a new `leasttime` load balancing strategy that selects backend servers based on average response time (TTFB) and active connection count, weighted by server capacity. \n \n### Motivation \n \nTraefik's existing strategies (WRR, P2C, HRW) don't consider response time/latency as a selection criterion. \nThe `leasttime` strategy routes traffic to the fastest-responding servers while maintaining fair load distribution. \nIt is particularly interesting when: \n- Backend servers have heterogeneous performance (different hardware, locations, or load) \n- Servers experience performance degradation (sustained load, network latency changes) \n- Multi-datacenter deployments with varying RTT \n \n### More \n \n- [x] Added/updated tests \n- [x] Added/updated documentation\n\n[...]\n\n- Review by lbenguigui: \n\n- rtribotte removed label \"status/0-needs-triage\"\n\n- rtribotte added label \"kind/enhancement\"\n\n- rtribotte added label \"status/2-needs-review\"\n\n- rtribotte added label \"area/service\"\n\n- rtribotte milestoned\n\n- rtribotte head_ref_force_pushed\n\n[...]\n\n/\n\n[...]\n\n- Renamed from \"feat: least time load balancing strategy\" to \"Add least time load balancing strategy\"\n\n- Review by rtribotte: LGTM\n\n- Review by kevinpollet: \n\n- kevinpollet removed label \"status/2-needs-review\"\n\n- kevinpollet added label \"status/3-needs-merge\"\n\n[...]\n\nrd\n-\n\n[...]\n\n- traefiker added label \"area/provider/k8s/crd\"\n\n- traefiker added label \"area/provider/k8s\"\n\n- traefiker added label \"size/L\"\n\n- traefiker added label \"status/0-needs-triage\""}}]},"finish_reason":null,"native_finish_reason":null}]}
data: {"id":"gen-1785177601-Q9kE2qjAwTQxa2yYaLnv","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1785177601,"model":"openai/gpt-5.6-terra","provider":"OpenAI","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"","role":"assistant","annotations":[{"type":"url_citation","url_citation":{"url":"https://github.com/traefik/traefik/commit/a754236ce501b63560cf241830bbe22cd1695f0e","title":"Add least time load balancing strategy · a754236 · traefik/traefik","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"## Add least time load balancing strategy\n\n- Author: @sdelicata\n- Committer: @web-flow\n- Date: 2025-10-23T14:16:05Z\n- SHA: a754236ce501b63560cf241830bbe22cd1695f0e\n- Changes: +1830 -134 (25 files)\n- Verified: yes\n\n[...]\n\n# Commit: traefik/traefik@a754236\n\n[...]\n\n- Repository: traefik/traefik | The Cloud Native Application Proxy | 63K stars | Go\n\n[...]\n\n@@ -515,3 +515,13 @@ For the experimental channel:\n ```shell\n kubectl apply -f https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/gateway-api/releases/download/v1.4.0/experimental-install.yaml\n ```\n+\n+### Kubernetes CRD Provider\n+\n+To use the new `leastime` load-balancer algorithm with the Kubernetes CRD provider, you need to update your CRDs.\n+\n+**Apply Updated CRDs:**\n+\n+```shell\n+kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/traefik/traefik/v3.6/docs/content/reference/dynamic-configuration/kubernetes-crd-definition-v1.yml\n+```\n```\n\n[...]\n\n```diff\n\n[...]\n\n### docs/content/migrate/v3.md\n\n[...]\n\n@@ -190,6 +190,12 @@ type WRRService struct {\n \tGRPCStatus *GRPCStatus `json:\"-\" toml:\"-\" yaml:\"-\" label:\"-\" file:\"-\"`\n }\n \n+// SetDefaults Default values for a WRRService.\n\n[...]\n\n@@ -204,12 +210,6 @@ func (w *HRWService) SetDefaults() {\n \tw.Weight = &defaultWeight\n }\n\n[...]\n\n+func (w *WRRService) SetDefaults() {\n+\tdefaultWeight :=\n\n[...]\n\n-// SetDefaults Default values for a WRRService.\n-func (w *WRRService) SetDefaults() {\n-\tdefaultWeight := 1\n-\tw.Weight = &defaultWeight\n-}\n-\n // +k8s:deepcopy-gen=true\n \n type GRPCStatus struct {\n\n[...]\n\n@@ -267,6 +267,8 @@ const (\n \tBalancerStrategyP2C BalancerStrategy = \"p2c\"\n \t// BalancerStrategyHRW is the highest random weight strategy.\n \tBalancerStrategyHRW BalancerStrategy = \"hrw\"\n+\t// BalancerStrategyLeastTime is the least-time strategy.\n+\tBalancerStrategyLeastTime BalancerStrategy = \"leasttime\"\n )\n \n // +k8s:deepcopy-gen=true\n```\n\n[...]\n\n+\n\n[...]\n\n```diff\n\n[...]\n\n1\n+\tw.Weight = &defaultWeight\n+}\n+\n // +k8s:deepcopy-gen=true\n \n // HRWService is a reference to a service load-balanced with highest random weight.\n\n[...]\n\n```diff\n\n[...]\n\nchoices algorithm is a load balancing strategy that selects two ser\n           url = \"http://private-ip-server-3/\"\n     ```\n \n+## Least-Time\n+\n+The Least-Time load balancing algorithm selects the server with the lowest average response time (Time To First Byte - TTFB),\n+combined with the fewest active connections, weighted by server capacity.\n+This strategy is ideal for heterogeneous backend environments where servers have varying performance characteristics,\n+different hardware capabilities, or varying network latency.\n+\n+The algorithm continuously measures each backend's response time and tracks active connection counts.\n\n[...]\n\n@@ -485,6 +485,48 @@ Power of\n\n[...]\n\n+When routing a request,\n+it calculates a score for each healthy server using the formula: `(avg_response_time × (1 + active_connections)) / weight`.\n+The server with the lowest score receives the request.\n+When multiple servers have identical scores,\n+Weighted Round Robin (WRR) with Earliest Deadline First (EDF) scheduling is used as a tie-breaker to ensure fair distribution.\n\n[...]\n\nyaml\n\n[...]\n\n```diff\n\n[...]\n\n+ ```"}}]},"finish_reason":null,"native_finish_reason":null}]}
